course: dictionary
lesson: 13046
title: Fascinated: wanting to know more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clues in the words around a word help you understand it. «Maya was fascinated by the dinosaur bones at the museum.» She read every sign and stayed for hours, so fascinated must mean very interested.
explain: Fascinated can also mean held so still that you cannot look away. «The cat was fascinated by the fish swimming in the tank.» The cat did not move at all, with its eyes fixed on the water, as if under a spell.
explain: Fascinate is the verb, and fascinating describes the thing that causes the feeling. «The volcano was fascinating.» The volcano is fascinating, but Maya is fascinated. Phrases to notice are «fascinated by» and «fascinated with».
fact: Fascinated means extremely interested in something, so you want to keep watching or learning about it.
fact: Fascinated can also mean held still by something you cannot stop looking at, as if under a spell.
fact: Fascinate is the verb, and fascinates, fascinated and fascinating are its other forms.
fact: «Fascinated» is often followed by «by» or «with»: fascinated by, fascinated with.
fact: Pupils are often fascinated by dinosaurs, space or volcanoes.
exercise: «Ravi was fascinated by the volcano.» What does fascinated mean? | Bored and ready to go home | *Extremely interested, wanting to keep learning about it | Frightened of loud noises | Hungry after a long day
exercise: «The children were fascinated, and nobody moved while the story was read.» What does fascinated mean here? | *Held still, as if under a spell | Bored of the story | Wide awake and ready to run | Very cross
exercise: What is the base verb of fascinated? | fashion | *fascinate | famous | faster
test: «The volcano was fascinating.» Which word describes the volcano itself? | *fascinating | fast | fascinated | famous
test: «Mia was fascinated with the stars.» What does this tell you about Mia? | Tired of looking up at the sky | Afraid of the dark | *Very interested in the stars and keen to learn more | Hungry for a snack
exam: Which sentence shows someone fascinated? | Leo dropped his bag and ran for the bus | Leo ate his lunch quickly | *Leo stared at the spider for ages, unable to look away | Leo yawned and went to sleep
